  "family": "Quillajaceae",
  "memo": "This tree has a rounded canopy filled with glossy, dark green leaves that provide ample shade. Its bark is rugged and has a distinctive, cork-like texture. In the spring, it produces small, white flowers that add a subtle touch of elegance to its appearance. The tree is drought-tolerant, making it well-suited for urban environments with limited water resources. It also has a moderate growth rate, ensuring it won't outgrow its space too quickly. This tree is an excellent choice for adding both beauty and resilience to city landscapes.",
