  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree has thick, evergreen leaves that stay vibrant year-round, making it a good subject for discussions on evergreen versus deciduous plants. The leaves contain saponins, which can be used to teach about natural soap production and chemical properties in plants. Its bark can be incorporated into lessons about traditional uses of plants by indigenous cultures. The tree produces clusters of small, white flowers that attract pollinators, providing opportunities to explore pollination and ecosystem interactions.",
